{"n": 619, "w": 1000, "h": 764, "img": "619.webp", "text": "33-1\n\n(325 IX): Checking Viscous Rear Axle Lock In Car:\n\nCéndition of viscous lock can be checked on brake test stand with BMW SER-\nVICE TESTER.\n\nCaution!\nHf only one wheel turns during tesf on brake test stand, viscous lock Is sub-\nJected to strong loads. This could lead to destruction due to excessive heat.\n\nTotal operation time = warming up time + fest time = 40 seconds on brake test\nstand must not be exceeded.\n\nBreak of at least 30 minutes Is required after each test. This time ts applicable\nto both cold and warm-run cars.\n\nCylinder speed of brake test stand must not excéed max, 7.5 km/h (4.5 mph).\nHf cylinder speed of brake test stand Is ‘not known, It can be determined with\n\nmethods described In test for a 3 series car with ABS, but without for wheel\ndrive. In $0 doing Warm-up phase and braking force are omitted.\n\neo i TN Check tire pressure and tire size.\n= Do not set brake test stand to auto-\n\n* See : Drive car on test stand with Its rear\n\nwheels on cylinders.\nSwitch off ignition.\nFront wheels on floor.\nShift lever In 1st gear.\n\nCar must be connected on BMW SER-\nVICE TESTER to determine test stand\nspeed (whee! speed) under load.\nSwitch off electric equipment items\n\nand ignition.\n\nConnect T-connector (4) between ABS\ncontrol unit (2) and ABS wire harness\n(1).\n\n30 27 003\n\n30.27 00\n\n30 27 005\n\n30 27 008\n\nPriifstand\n\nSelect Test Program 03 ABS on BMW\nSERVICE TESTER.\nSelect ABS Test Step 03.\n\nSwitch on one brake test stand cyl-\nInder and let It run about 30 seconds\n(warm-up phase).\n\nPress confirmation button on BMW\nSERVICE TESTER after warm-up time.\nValue now displayed In ms Is the cyl-\nInder speed for left or right rear.\n\nSee diagram.\n\nRead braking force of left or right\nwhee! on brake test stand.\n\nimportant!\nTotal operation time = max. 40 seconds.", "words": [["33-1", 0.4489, 0.0152, 0.5349, 0.0417], ["(325", 0.0521, 0.0866, 0.0743